><surname>Bennett</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Adducin is an in vivo substrate for protein kinase Cphosphorylation in the MARCKS-related domain inhibits activity in promoting spectrin&#x02013;actin complexes and occurs in many cells, including dendritic spines of neurons</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>142</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>485</fpage><lpage>497</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9679146</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Mikietal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miki</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sasaki</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Takai</surname><given-names>Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Takenawa</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Induction of filopodium formation by a WASP-related actin-depolymerizing protein N-WASP</article-title><source>Nature.</source><volume>391</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>96</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9422512</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="MitchisonandKirschner1988"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mitchison</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirschner</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cytoskeletal dynamics and nerve growth</article-title><source>Neuron</source><volume>1</volume><year>1988</year><fpage>761</fpage><lpage>772</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3078414</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="MitchisonandCramer1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mitchison</surname><given-names>T.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cramer</surname><given-names>L.P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Actin-based cell motility and cell locomotion</article-title><source>Cell.</source><volume>84</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>371</fpage><lpage>379</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8608590</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Mitchisonetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mitchison</surname><given-names>T.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sawin</surname><given-names>K.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Theriot</surname><given-names>J.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gee</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mallavarapu</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Caged fluorescent probes</article-title><source>Methods Enzymol</source><volume>291</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>78</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9661145</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="MyersandBastiani1993"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Myers</surname><given-names>P.Z.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bastiani</surname><given-names>M.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Growth cone dynamics during the migration of an identified commissural growth cone</article-title><source>J. Neurosci.</source><volume>13</volume><year>1993</year><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>143</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8423468</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="OConnoretal1990"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O'Connor</surname><given-names>T.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Duerr</surname><given-names>J.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bentley</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pioneer growth cone steering decisions mediated by single filopodium contacts in situ</article-title><source>J. Neurosci</source><volume>10</volume><year>1990</year><fpage>3935</fpage><lpage>3946</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2269892</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Ohtaetal1999"><citation citation-type="jou